 to MHCnuggets! Presumably you're here to do some\npeptide-MHC prediction and not because you were [hungry](https://www.mcdonalds.com/us/en-us/product/chicken-mcnuggets-4-piece.html).\n\n### Usage ###\nFor an overview of how to use MHCnuggets please refer to the Jupyter notebook\ncalled `user_guide.ipynb` in the repository\n\n### Installation ###\n\nMHCnuggets is `pip` installable as:\n```bash\npip install mhcnuggets\n```\n\n**Required pacakges:**\n\n* numpy\n* scipy\n* scikit-learn\n* tensorflow\n* keras\n\nYou might want to check if the Keras backend is configured to use\nthe Tensforflow backend.","build":{"noarch":"python","number":1,"run_exports":[null],"script":"-m pip install . --no-deps --no-build-isolation --no-cache-dir -vvv"},"requirements":{"host":["pip","python","setuptools"],"run":["keras >=2.6,<3","numpy","pandas","python","scikit-learn","scipy","tensorflow >=2.6,<2.16","varcode"]},"source_url":"https://pypi.io/packages/source/m/mhcnuggets/mhcnuggets-2.4.1.tar.gz","test":{"imports":["mhcnuggets","mhcnuggets.data","mhcnuggets.data.production","mhcnuggets.data.production.mhcI","mhcnuggets.data.production.mhcII","mhcnuggets.data.test","mhcnuggets.saves","mhcnuggets.saves.production","mhcnuggets.saves.test","mhcnuggets.src"]},"recipe_maintainers":["jonasscheid"]}}}